B.a6B=new A.mU('What "reviewed" means here \u2014 and what it does not','Every dose in this app was checked against a named clinical guideline, and the guideline is shown beside the dose so you can go and read it.\n\nOn 24 August 2026 the physician who builds and maintains this app approved that content. He is a practising doctor, so that is a real clinical sign-off, and it is why entries read "reviewed" rather than only "verified".\n\nIt is not an independent review by a second clinician, an editorial board, or a specialty society, and it was given for the body of content rather than as a fresh line-by-line audit of all 766 conditions on that date. Where you would normally trust a reference book because a named editor stood behind it, here you should trust the citation and check it when it matters.',null)
B.a6C=new A.mU("The scores and calculators","The clinical scores \u2014 Centor, Wells, PHQ-9, CHA\u2082DS\u2082-VASc, the Ottawa rules and the rest \u2014 apply exactly the criteria their published source states, and output a risk band and what that source says to do. They never output a drug dose. Each shows its criteria and its citation on the same screen.\n\nBMI and Albak Amana are the same: arithmetic you could do yourself, and a chart lookup, both naming their source.\n\nA child\u2019s dose is shown as the published mg/kg rule, with that rule worked out at fixed weights beneath it, one row per kilogram from 3 to 50 kg. Those figures are our arithmetic on the printed rule, not a table quoted from a guideline, and the screen says so. Typing a weight or an age highlights the row of that table it lands on \u2014 it never works out a number of its own, and a weight between two rows highlights both rather than rounding to one.",null)
B.a6D=new A.mU("Your data, and the one thing that leaves this device","The app holds no account. Your favourites, your recent lookups, the brands you marked as unavailable and anything you type into a calculator are stored on this device only, and are deleted with the app.\n\nOne thing does leave this device, and only when you ask for it: the message you type into the report-a-problem box. Tapping Send delivers that message to the developer, together with the app version and which screen you were on. Nothing is sent unless you tap Send, and nothing else is ever sent.\n\nNothing you enter about a patient is recorded, and no patient identity is asked for anywhere.\n\nThis is a reference for prescribers. It is not a medical device and it does not diagnose, treat, cure or prevent any condition \u2014 it reports what named guidelines say, and the clinical decision remains yours.",null)
B.a6E=new A.mU("Prices and brands","Egyptian trade names and prices come from the national drug register. Prices move and the register lags behind the pharmacy shelf, so treat every figure as an indication, not a quotation. A product being listed does not mean it is in stock, and a product being absent does not mean it is gone.",null)
B.a6F=new A.mU("Reporting something wrong","If a dose here does not match the guideline it cites, that is a defect and it matters more than any feature. Note the condition and the drug and report it.",null)
B.a6G=new A.mU("Where the content comes from","NICE guidelines \xb7 the Egyptian National Drug Formulary \xb7 the Egyptian Essential Medicines List \xb7 WHO model formularies \xb7 disease-specific society guidance such as IDSA and GOLD.\n\nEvery condition page lists the specific sources behind it. Where we could not source something, the app says so instead of filling the gap.",null)
